---
// A fictional example explains the mechanism; measured results follow separately.
---
<section class="recall-explorer" aria-labelledby="recall-explorer-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="recall-intro">
      <div><p class="overline">Inside the idea · illustrative example</p><h2 id="recall-explorer-title">The answer is stored.<br /><span>The connection is missing.</span></h2></div>
      <p>A search can find the note about the garden and miss the note that answers the question. Follow the designer’s name to see what changes.</p>
    </header>
    <fieldset class="recall-demo">
      <legend>Choose how to look for the answer</legend>
      <input type="radio" name="recall-route" id="recall-direct" checked />
      <label for="recall-direct">01 · Search the question</label>
      <input type="radio" name="recall-route" id="recall-bridge" />
      <label for="recall-bridge">02 · Follow the connection</label>
      <div class="recall-scene">
        <div class="recall-query"><span>The question</span><p>Where was the garden’s designer born?</p></div>
        <div class="recall-path">
          <article class="recall-document"><span>Note A · found</span><h3>The garden</h3><p>The garden was designed by <strong>Mira Vale</strong>.</p><small>A name gives us the next thing to search for.</small></article>
          <div class="recall-edge" aria-hidden="true"><span class="direct-copy">No direct match</span><span class="bridge-copy">Search “Mira Vale”</span><b>→</b></div>
          <article class="recall-document recall-target"><span class="direct-copy">Note B · outside the results</span><span class="bridge-copy">Note B · reached through the name</span><h3>Mira Vale</h3><p>Mira Vale was born in <strong>Harbor Bay</strong>.</p><small>The answer was already in the archive.</small></article>
        </div>
        <p class="recall-explanation direct-copy"><strong>Direct retrieval:</strong> the question mentions the garden, but the answer note does not. In this example, similarity search misses it.</p>
        <p class="recall-explanation bridge-copy"><strong>Follow the connection:</strong> use the name from Note A to reach Note B. The intermediate note changes what we search for.</p>
      </div>
    </fieldset>
    <p class="recall-footnote">Invented names and notes, shown to explain two-hop retrieval. This is not a benchmark example or a live retriever; real retrieval may succeed or fail differently.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .recall-explorer { margin:0; padding:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem) 0; background:#17243a; color:#f4f6fc; }
  .recall-intro { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr; gap:3rem; align-items:end; margin-bottom:2rem; }
  .recall-intro .overline { color:#a9c5ff; }
  h2 { margin:.9rem 0 0; font:500 clamp(2rem,4vw,3.6rem)/1.05 var(--serif); letter-spacing:-.04em; }
  h2 span { color:#acc9ff; }
  .recall-intro > p { color:#d0daea; line-height:1.65; max-width:42ch; margin:0; }
  .recall-demo { padding:0; border:0; margin:0; min-width:0; }
  legend { color:#d0daea; font-size:.8rem; margin-bottom:1rem; }
  input { position:absolute; opacity:0; width:1px; height:1px; }
  label { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; min-height:48px; padding:.65rem 1rem; margin:0 .5rem .6rem 0; border:1px solid #8295b3; border-radius:6px; cursor:pointer; font-size:.85rem; }
  input:checked + label { background:#dce8ff; color:#17243a; border-color:#dce8ff; font-weight:650; }
  input:focus-visible + label { outline:3px solid #ffc777; outline-offset:4px; }
  .recall-scene { margin-top:1rem; border:1px solid #8295b3; border-radius:10px; padding:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem); background:#1c2d46; }
  .recall-query { border-bottom:1px solid #8295b3; padding-bottom:1.25rem; margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
  .recall-query span,.recall-document > span { font:500 .72rem/1.5 var(--mono); color:#c0d5fc; }
  .recall-query p { margin:.5rem 0 0; font:500 clamp(1.25rem,2.5vw,1.8rem)/1.3 var(--serif); }
  .recall-path { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 150px minmax(0,1fr); align-items:stretch; gap:1rem; }
  .recall-document { padding:1.4rem; border:1px solid #a6c4fa; border-radius:6px; background:#243c60; }
  .recall-document h3 { font:500 1.6rem/1.2 var(--serif); margin:1rem 0; }
  .recall-document p { line-height:1.6; }
  .recall-document strong { color:#ffe0ac; }
  .recall-document small { display:block; color:#d0daea; font-size:.8rem; line-height:1.5; }
  .recall-target { border-style:dashed; background:#1c2d46; }
  .recall-edge { align-self:center; text-align:center; font-size:.8rem; line-height:1.5; color:#d0daea; }
  .recall-edge b { display:block; font-size:2rem; }
  .recall-explanation { margin:1.5rem 0 0; padding:1rem 0 0; border-top:1px solid #8295b3; line-height:1.65; color:#e0e8f6; }
  .bridge-copy { display:none; }
  #recall-bridge:checked ~ .recall-scene .direct-copy { display:none; }
  #recall-bridge:checked ~ .recall-scene .bridge-copy { display:block; }
  #recall-bridge:checked ~ .recall-scene .recall-target { border-style:solid; background:#243c60; }
  #recall-bridge:checked ~ .recall-scene .recall-edge { color:#ffe0ac; }
  .recall-footnote { margin:1rem 0 0; color:#c5d2e5; font-size:.8rem; line-height:1.6; max-width:90ch; }
  @media(max-width:700px) {
    .recall-intro,.recall-path { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:1.25rem; }
    .recall-edge b { transform:rotate(90deg); }
    label { display:flex; margin-right:0; }
  }
</style>
